**Key idea:** Make the burst size a **`rand` field of the sequence** with a `soft` default constraint, loop `burst_size` times in `body()`, and let whoever starts the sequence decide the value at run time: inline `randomize() with {}` from the test or virtual sequence, a `uvm_config_db` lookup at the start of `body()`, or a shared config object that another component updates during simulation.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant T as test or virtual sequence
  participant S as burst_seq
  participant Q as sequencer
  participant D as driver
  T->>S: randomize with burst_size == n
  T->>S: start on sequencer
  S->>S: body reads config_db override if present
  loop burst_size times
    S->>Q: start_item / finish_item
    Q->>D: item i, last when i == n-1
  end
  S-->>T: start returns
```

### Code
```systemverilog
class burst_seq extends uvm_sequence #(bus_item);
  `uvm_object_utils(burst_seq)
  rand int unsigned burst_size;
  constraint c_size { soft burst_size inside {[1:16]}; }   // default, easy to override

  function new(string name = "burst_seq"); super.new(name); endfunction

  task body();
    int unsigned n;
    // Optional run-time override published by the test, a plusarg handler or another component
    if (uvm_config_db#(int unsigned)::get(m_sequencer, "", "burst_size", n))
      burst_size = n;
    `uvm_info("BURST", $sformatf("starting burst of %0d", burst_size), UVM_MEDIUM)
    for (int i = 0; i < burst_size; i++) begin
      req = bus_item::type_id::create($sformatf("req%0d", i));
      start_item(req);
      if (!req.randomize() with { beat == i; last == (i == local::burst_size - 1); })
        `uvm_error("RAND", "bus_item randomization failed")
      finish_item(req);
    end
  endtask
endclass

class burst_test extends base_test;
  `uvm_component_utils(burst_test)
  function new(string name, uvm_component parent); super.new(name, parent); endfunction

  task main_phase(uvm_phase phase);
    int unsigned sizes[$] = '{1, 4, 16, 256};
    int unsigned extra;
    phase.raise_objection(this);
    if ($value$plusargs("BURST=%d", extra)) sizes.push_back(extra);   // decided at run time
    foreach (sizes[k]) begin
      burst_seq s = burst_seq::type_id::create($sformatf("burst%0d", k));
      // inline constraint overrides the soft default
      if (!s.randomize() with { burst_size == local::sizes[k]; })
        `uvm_fatal("RAND", "burst_seq randomization failed")
      s.start(env.agt.sqr);
    end
    phase.drop_objection(this);
  endtask
endclass
```

### Explanation
- `soft` lets callers override the default range without a constraint conflict.
- `local::` in the inline constraint forces the name to resolve in the caller's scope, not inside the randomized object.
- For truly dynamic behavior (burst size tracking DUT state), pass the sequence a handle to a config object or a monitor-fed variable and re-read it **before each burst**, not once at construction.
- Mark the last beat (`last`) so the driver can assert `xLAST`/end-of-burst signals.

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- `burst_size == 0`: decide whether it is legal (empty loop) or constrain it to `>= 1`.
- Very large values: add a hard upper bound from the protocol (for example AXI4 INCR max 256 beats).
- A config_db `get` with a mismatched type (`int` vs `int unsigned`) silently misses the override.
- If another sequence may `lock` the sequencer, a burst can be interleaved unless this sequence also locks.

### Follow-ups
- *How to keep a burst atomic?* Call `lock(m_sequencer)` before the loop and `unlock(m_sequencer)` after.
- *How to verify all sizes were used?* A covergroup on `burst_size` with bins for 1, max, and ranges in between, sampled in `body()`.
